---

<DocsPage
  title="Not built yet"
  description="What the plans still hold, grouped by epic. A snapshot taken on 2026-10-17."
>
  <DocSection title="How to read this page">
    <p>
      The work is tracked in Colby Maestro under the project key <code>core-shopping</code>, as three plans: a contract
      plan, a frontend plan and a backend plan. Maestro is the live record. This page is a snapshot, so check Maestro
      before relying on any line here.
    </p>
    <p>
      Done so far: the platform and database, the schema, the goals, runs and sightings routes, browser-run plumbing, the goals
      console, the Overview, and the run queue and run detail pages. Everything below is what remains. Backend items come
      first, because the interface cannot show what nothing yet writes.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection title="Backend and data" description="Largest gap first." flush>
    <DocRows rows={backend} />
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection title="Interface" description="Pages that are placeholders today." flush>
    <DocRows rows={frontend} />
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection
    title="Requests in the brief that the plans had no home for"
    description="Found by auditing the plans against the brief, then filed as tasks tagged spec-gap."
    flush
  >
    <DocRows rows={gaps} />
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection title="Known bugs" description="Open in Maestro." flush>
    <DocRows rows={bugs} />
  </DocSection>
</DocsPage>
